# Front-End Dev-Mode: Advanced Implementation

## Purpose

This file provides comprehensive guidance for advanced front-end implementation tasks that involve complex architecture, state management, and component interactions. It is designed for complex user interface features, advanced state management patterns, and sophisticated component hierarchies.

## Usage as Project-Rule-Parameter

This file contains advanced implementation patterns for front-end development and should be referenced as a project-rule-parameter in message-commands when implementing complex front-end features:

```
dev-mode: front-end-workflow @parameters/front-end/dev-mode/dev-mode-advanced.mdc
```

## Mode Activation

When activated with:

```
dev-mode: front-end-workflow @parameters/front-end/dev-mode/dev-mode-advanced.mdc
```

This parameter enables:
- Comprehensive component architecture analysis
- Advanced state management implementation
- Complex UI feature development
- Integration with back-end API systems
- Advanced testing and verification patterns

## Implementation Strategy

The advanced implementation strategy follows a structured, architectural approach:

### 1. Architecture Analysis Phase

Start with a comprehensive analysis of the architecture to understand component relationships, data flow, and state management:

```typescript
// 1. Access architecture knowledge
fetch_rules(["knowledge/reference/architecture"], 
           "Understanding system architecture for implementation")

// 2. Understand component structure
codebase_search("component structure pattern", ["front-end/src/components"])

// 3. Examine state management approach
grep_search("createContext|useReducer|useState", false, "*.tsx")

// 4. Analyze routing structure
read_file("front-end/src/App.tsx", should_read_entire_file=true)

// 5. Understand API integration
codebase_search("API integration pattern", ["front-end/src/api"])
```

### 2. Component Hierarchy Implementation

Implement the component hierarchy with proper abstraction, composition, and inheritance patterns:

```typescript
// 1. Start with container components
edit_file("front-end/src/components/Container.tsx", 
          "Implement container component architecture",
          "// Container component implementation...")

// 2. Build feature-specific components
edit_file("front-end/src/components/Feature/index.tsx", 
          "Implement feature components",
          "// Feature component implementation...")

// 3. Create reusable UI components
edit_file("front-end/src/components/UI/Component.tsx", 
          "Implement reusable UI components",
          "// UI component implementation...")

// 4. Implement functionality-specific sub-components
edit_file("front-end/src/components/Feature/SubComponent.tsx", 
          "Implement functionality-specific sub-components",
          "// Sub-component implementation...")
```

### 3. State Management Implementation

